; Title screen attributes: rows 0-15, 32 bytes per row
;
; Attributes of the upper two thirds of the title screen (16 rows of 32 bytes,
; row 0 first). #R$87CA copies $300 bytes from here to $5800, so the attributes
; of the third part of the title screen come from #R$9A00 (the status bar
; colours). It then reads the copy on the screen to decide what to draw in each
; cell:
; .
; $00 black, nothing drawn. $D3 (flash, bright red paper, magenta ink): the big
; letters "JET SET WILLY", cells without pixels, the red paper is the letter.
; $09, $24, $2D: solid blue, green and cyan blocks of the picture, also without
; pixels. The drawing loop skips exactly these five values.
; $08, $29, $05 and $2C (the last stored back as $25) are drawn with the edge
; pieces +0/+8 of #R$8431; any other attribute ($28, $25, $04 occur in this
; data) with the pieces +$10/+$18. Taken from the code of #R$87CA; the result is
; the triangle of the title screenshot (blue, green and cyan faces).
@label=TitleAttributes
b$9800 DEFS $52
